        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_completion_tokens": 32000,
                "reasoning_effort": "medium"
              },
              "code": "ORA_MODEL_CONFIG_PREMIUM_OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "model": "OCI_GPT_5_MINI",
              "modelName": "Gpt-5 Mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "name": "Bundle Components Scoring Assistant"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1773306829766"
          },
          "code": "ORA_CX_ENTERPRISE_BUNDLE_COMPONENTS_SCORING_ASSISTANT",
          "id": "1770195103364",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770195103365_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a COMPONENT SIMILARITY DETECTION & RANKING ENGINE.\nYour job is to compare components of a QUERY against components of multiple CANDIDATES and compute:\n1. A deterministic similarity score (0–40 only)\n2. A strict ranking with deterministic tie-breakers\n3. Structured reasoning (no counts, no math, no business impact)\n4. Component match metadata for downstream use\nYou must focus ONLY on components.\nDo NOT evaluate product info, specifications, characteristics, validity, rules, or pricing.\nYou must process ALL CANDIDATES provided.\nThis is a strict batch processing task.\n=========================================================\nINPUT CONTEXT\n=========================================================\nQUERY = {{$context.$nodes.ORA_CX_ENTERPRISE_DETERMINE_VECTOR_QUERY.$output.result}}\nCANDIDATES = {{$context.$nodes.ORA_CX_ENTERPRISE_VECTORIZED_OFFER_READER.$output}}\nCANDIDATES is an ARRAY of CANDIDATE objects.\nYou MUST iterate through EVERY object inside CANDIDATES.\nDo NOT skip, summarize, merge, or truncate any CANDIDATE.\nProcess each CANDIDATE independently.\n=========================================================\nSTRICT FIELD MAPPING\n=========================================================\nFor EACH CANDIDATE in CANDIDATES:\ncandidate_id               = CANDIDATE['OfferDetails']['ID']\ncandidate_name             = CANDIDATE['OfferDetails']['Name']\ncandidate_productType      = CANDIDATE['OfferDetails']['Type']\ncandidate_components       = CANDIDATE['Components']['List']\ncandidate_validity_end = If CANDIDATE['Validity']['endDateTime'] is empty then Infinity or CANDIDATE['Validity']['endDateTime’]\n\nQuery fields:\nquery_id                   = QUERY['OfferDetails']['ID']\nquery_name                 = QUERY['OfferDetails']['Name']\nquery_productType          = QUERY['OfferDetails']['Type']\nquery_components           = QUERY['Components']['List']\nquery_validity_start = QUERY['Validity']['startDateTime’]\n\nIMPORTANT CLARIFICATION\n- productOfferingTerm is evaluated only when present inside individual component objects within Components['List'], not at the offer level.\n- When present, productOfferingTerm represents the component’s overridden commitment term.\n=========================================================\nPROCESSING FLOW\n=========================================================\nSTEP 1 — TYPE FILTER\nEligible CANDIDATES:\n- candidate_productType == query_productType\n- candidate_id != query_id\n- query_validity_start < candidate_validity_end\nCANDIDATES failing this filter must still be returned in output\nwith final_score = 0 and rank assigned accordingly.\n\nSTEP 2 — Normalize Query Components\nFor each Parent Offer component in query_components, extract normalized fields:\n- component_name_normalized (lowercase, trim spaces, remove formatting noise)\n- cardinality (minOccurs, maxOccurs) normalized into consistent representation\n- component_role:\n  - CORE (Mandatory) if minOccurs ≥ 1\n  - OPTIONAL if minOccurs = 0\n- component_type (if inferable): Physical good / Service / Digital / Add-on / Usage-based / Other\n- overridden_commitment_term_normalized (optional, per component)\n  - Source: component['productOfferingTerm']\n  - Interpret as the component’s overridden commitment term\n  - If present, normalize (lowercase, trim spaces, remove formatting noise)\n  - If missing or null, set to null\n  - Ignore href, IDs, validity dates, and pricing in or under this field\n\nIgnore href, IDs, validity dates, and pricing (including any such fields nested anywhere).\nTreat ordering-only differences as equivalent (sort consistently).\n\nSTEP 3 — Normalize CANDIDATE Components\nApply the same normalization and extraction as Parent Offer for each Compared Offer component, including:\n- overridden_commitment_term_normalized extracted from component['productOfferingTerm'] using the same rules\n\nSTEP 4 — Component Matching\nMatch each Parent Offer component against Compared Offer components using semantic intent.\n\nAllowed match strengths:\n- EXACT    = 1.0\n- SEMANTIC = 0.85\n- PARTIAL  = 0.55\n- WEAK     = 0.30\n- NONE     = 0.0\n\nOVERRIDDEN COMMITMENT TERM MATCH ADJUSTMENT (per component match; applies only if term exists on either side)\nFor a given Parent Offer component matched to a Compared Offer component:\n- If both have overridden_commitment_term_normalized and they are equivalent, keep match strength as-is\n- If both have overridden_commitment_term_normalized and they conflict, downgrade match strength by one level:\n  - EXACT → SEMANTIC\n  - SEMANTIC → PARTIAL\n  - PARTIAL → WEAK\n  - WEAK → NONE\n- If Parent Offer has overridden_commitment_term_normalized but Compared Offer does not, downgrade match strength by one level\n- If Compared Offer has overridden_commitment_term_normalized but Parent Offer does not, do not downgrade\n\nTrack the following as LISTS of component names only (no prose, no IDs):\n- exactMatches\n- semanticMatches\n- partialMatches\n- weakMatches\n- missingCoreComponents\n- missingOptionalComponents\n- extraComponents\n- commitmentTermAlignedComponents\n- commitmentTermMismatchedOrMissingComponents\n\nAlso compute:\n- matched_components (all matches except NONE)\n- missing_components (missingCoreComponents + missingOptionalComponents)\n\n=========================================================\nSCORING MODEL (0–40)\n=========================================================\nIgnore all href fields in scoring.\n================\nPOSITIVE BLOCK (TOTAL MAX 40)\n================\nCOMPONENTS — MAX 40\nIf both sides contain components:\n  component_score =\n    (sum(match_strengths_per_query_component) / max(1, total_query_components)) * 40\nElse if both absent:\n  component_score = 40\npositive_total = component_score\n\n================\nGRANULAR DEDUCTIONS (ADJUSTED FOR 0–40)\n================\nDeductions apply ONLY when components exist on at least one side.\n\nCOMPONENTS — MAX 16\ncomponents_deduction =\n  min(16,\n    (missing_components_count + extra_components_count) * 1.5\n  )\n\nOVERRIDDEN COMMITMENT TERM — MAX 6\ncommitment_term_deduction =\n  min(6,\n    commitmentTermMismatchedOrMissingComponents_count * 1.0\n  )\n\ntotal_deduction = components_deduction + commitment_term_deduction\n\n=========================================================\nFINAL SCORE\n=========================================================\nfinal_score =\n  clamp(0, 40,\n    positive_total - total_deduction\n  )\nScore must be numeric between 0 and 40.\n\n=========================================================\nTERMINOLOGY RULES (UI-FRIENDLY)\n=========================================================\nUse:\n- \"Parent Offer\" for \"Query\"\n- \"Compared Offer\" for \"Candidate\"\nNever use:\nQUERY, CANDIDATE, vector, score calculation, penalty, weight\n\n=========================================================\nREASONING RULES (UPDATED)\n=========================================================\nFor each CANDIDATE, strictly follow the format below and avoid all href from reasoning.\n=========================================================\nSimilarities (Include all 3 points)\n=========================================================\nCore Components:\n  Describe CORE (mandatory) components that are shared between the Parent Offer and the Compared Offer.\n  Mention component type when helpful (e.g., service, add-on, physical).\nOptional Components:\n  Describe OPTIONAL components that are common between the two offers,\n  focusing on functional purpose rather than exact structure.\nOption Groups:\n  Describe option groups or aggregates that exist in BOTH the Parent Offer and the Compared Offer,\n  focusing on their functional purpose rather than internal structure.\n\n=========================================================\nDifferences (Include all 4 points)\n=========================================================\nMissing Core Components:\n  Clearly list mandatory components present in the Parent Offer but not included in the Compared Offer.\n  Emphasize functional impact without stating business outcomes.\nMissing Optional Components:\n  List optional components present in the Parent Offer but not included in the Compared Offer,\n  describing them as gaps or exclusions rather than defects.\nAdditional Components:\n  List extra components included in the Compared Offer,\n  describing them as extensions or enrichments when appropriate.\n  When applicable, mention that some additional components introduce different overridden commitment terms.\nOption Groups:\n  Describe option groups that are:\n  • present in the Parent Offer but missing in the Compared Offer, OR\n  • present in the Compared Offer but not in the Parent Offer.\n  Focus on functional differences rather than structure or hierarchy.\n  When applicable, mention differences in overridden commitment term handling across option groups.\n\n-----------------\nGLOBAL CONSTRAINTS\n-----------------\n- Do NOT mention:\n  - IDs, names, types, validity dates\n  - Scores, weights, penalties, counts, or calculations\n  - Business impact or recommendations\n- Keep total reasoning under 300 words\n- Reasoning should always end with a period(\".\")\n- Use clear, business-friendly language suitable for UI display\n- Reasoning should always be a comparison study of both offers and do not list just components\n- When overridden commitment terms are relevant:\n  - You may state alignment or mismatch only\n  - Do NOT display the term value itself (no durations, numbers, months, years)\n\n=========================================================\nIMPORTANT\n=========================================================\n- Mandatory vs optional distinction MUST be visible in reasoning\n- Language MUST be symmetric regardless of comparison direction\n- Similar offers should naturally read as similar even if small differences exist\n\n=========================================================\nOUTPUT REQUIREMENT (CRITICAL)\n=========================================================\nThis is a strict batch task.\n- You MUST return one result object per item in CANDIDATES\n- Important: Do not use \":\" anywhere in the reasoning other than after Core Components,Optional Components,Option Groups,Missing Core Components,Missing Optional Components and Additional Components.\n- The number of output objects MUST EXACTLY equal the length of CANDIDATES\n- Do NOT stop early\n- Do NOT merge CANDIDATES\n- Do NOT summarize multiple CANDIDATES\n- Output must be a pure JSON array"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"candidates\": [\n      {\n        \"candidate_id\": CANDIDATE['OfferDetails']['ID'],\n        \"candidate_name\": CANDIDATE['OfferDetails']['Name'],\n        \"score\": number,\n        \"productType\": CANDIDATE['OfferDetails']['Type'],\n        \"lifecycleStatus\": CANDIDATE['OfferDetails']['LifecycleStatus'],\n        \"reasoning\": {\n          \"Similarities\": \"Convert content including subheading in exact format mentioned in template into user language code {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.userDetails.Language}}\",\n          \"Differences\": \"Convert content including subheading  in exact format mentioned in template into user language code {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.userDetails.Language}}\"\n        }\n      }\n    ]\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Merge Product Offering Summaries for Bundle",
            "returnType": "array",
            "sourceCode": "// Inputs (each in the format you provided)\nconst llm1 = $context.$nodes.ORA_CX_ENTERPRISE_BUNDLE_COMPONENTS_SCORING_ASSISTANT.$output;\nconst llm2 = $context.$nodes.ORA_CX_ENTERPRISE_BUNDLE_PRICING_SCORING_ASSISTANT.$output;\nlet llm3 = $context.$nodes.ORA_CX_ENTERPRISE_BUNDLE_RULE_SCORING_ASSISTANT.$output;\nif( $context.$triggers.REST.$input.avoidProductRule ) {\n  llm3.score = 20;\n}\nconst llm4 = $context.$nodes.ORA_CX_ENTERPRISE_BUNDLE_PRODUCT_INFORMATION_SCORING_ASSISTANT.$output;\n\n// Merge\nconst byId = {};\nconst all = [llm1, llm2, llm3, llm4];\n\nfor (let llmIndex = 0; llmIndex < all.length; llmIndex++) {\n  const llm = all[llmIndex];\n  const candidates = (llm && Array.isArray(llm.candidates)) ? llm.candidates : [];\n\n  // Track duplicates *within the same LLM output* by candidate_id\n  // If duplicates exist, we keep only one set of reasoning fragments and one score per fragment-set.\n  // Score rule here: for duplicates of same candidate_id in same LLM, take the MAX score (avoid double counting).\n  const seenIdsInThisLLM = new Set();\n\n  // Additionally, track whether we already added a given reasoning fragment for this candidate within this LLM,\n  // so duplicates within the same LLM won't inflate score (optional but safer).\n  const seenSimFragKey = new Set();  // key: `${id}||S||${frag}`\n  const seenDiffFragKey = new Set(); // key: `${id}||D||${frag}`\n\n  for (const c of candidates) {\n    const id = c && c.candidate_id;\n    if (id == null) continue;\n\n    if (!byId[id]) {\n      byId[id] = {\n        candidate_id: id,\n        candidate_name: c.candidate_name,\n        productType: c.productType,\n        lifecycleStatus: c.lifecycleStatus,\n        score: 0,\n        _simSet: new Set(),\n        _diffSet: new Set(),\n        // used to apply \"max per LLM per candidate\" de-dupe\n        _perLLMMaxScore: {} // llmIndex -> maxScore\n      };\n    }\n\n    // ---- Score de-dupe within the same LLM for the same candidate_id ----\n    const s = Number(c.score);\n    const score = Number.isFinite(s) ? s : 0;\n\n    const prevMax = byId[id]._perLLMMaxScore[llmIndex];\n    if (prevMax == null || score > prevMax) {\n      // adjust total by delta between new max and old max (or old max=0 if none)\n      const old = prevMax == null ? 0 : prevMax;\n      byId[id].score += (score - old);\n      byId[id]._perLLMMaxScore[llmIndex] = score;\n    }\n\n    // ---- Reasoning de-dupe (within LLM and across LLMs) ----\n    const simRaw = (c.reasoning && typeof c.reasoning.Similarities === \"string\") ? c.reasoning.Similarities : \"\";\n    const diffRaw = (c.reasoning && typeof c.reasoning.Differences === \"string\") ? c.reasoning.Differences : \"\";\n\n    const simClean = simRaw.replace(/^\\s*Similarities\\s*:\\s*/i, \"\").trim();\n    const diffClean = diffRaw.replace(/^\\s*Differences\\s*:\\s*/i, \"\").trim();\n\n    // Split on newlines or bullets; keep unique non-empty fragments\n    const simParts = simClean ? simClean.split(/\\r?\\n|•|- /g) : [];\n    for (const part of simParts) {\n      const p = part.trim();\n      if (!p) continue;\n\n      const k = id + \"||S||\" + p;\n      if (!seenSimFragKey.has(k)) {\n        // prevent duplicates inside the same LLM output\n        seenSimFragKey.add(k);\n        // prevent duplicates across LLMs\n        byId[id]._simSet.add(p);\n      }\n    }\n\n    const diffParts = diffClean ? diffClean.split(/\\r?\\n|•|- /g) : [];\n    for (const part of diffParts) {\n      const p = part.trim();\n      if (!p) continue;\n\n      const k = id + \"||D||\" + p;\n      if (!seenDiffFragKey.has(k)) {\n        seenDiffFragKey.add(k);\n        byId[id]._diffSet.add(p);\n      }\n    }\n\n    seenIdsInThisLLM.add(id);\n  }\n}\n\n// Build final array\nconst mergedCandidates = Object.values(byId).map(x => {\n  const total = Math.round((x.score + Number.EPSILON) * 100) / 100;\n\n  let rank_class = \"LOW_SIMILARITY\";\n  if (total === 100) rank_class = \"EXACT_MATCH\";\n  else if (total >= 85 && total < 100) rank_class = \"HIGH_SIMILARITY\";\n  else if (total >= 65 && total < 85) rank_class = \"MOSTLY_SIMILAR\";\n  else if (total >= 45 && total < 65) rank_class = \"PARTIALLY_SIMILAR\";\n\n  return {\n    candidate_id: x.candidate_id,\n    candidate_name: x.candidate_name,\n    score: total,\n    productType: x.productType,\n    lifecycleStatus: x.lifecycleStatus,\n    reasoning: {\n      // Ensures \"Similarities:\" / \"Differences:\" are NOT repeated inside these fields\n      Similarities: Array.from(x._simSet).join(\"\\n\"),\n      Differences: Array.from(x._diffSet).join(\"\\n\")\n    },\n    rank_class\n  };\n});\n\n// Sort + rank (descending score)\nmergedCandidates.sort((a, b) => b.score - a.score);\nfor (let i = 0; i < mergedCandidates.length; i++) {\n  mergedCandidates[i].rank = i + 1;\n}\n\n// Final output\nconst finalOutput = { candidates: mergedCandidates };\nreturn finalOutput;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "ORA_CX_ENTERPRISE_MERGE_PRODUCT_OFFERING_SUMMARIES_FOR_BUNDLE",
          "id": "1773306829766",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_completion_tokens": 32000,
                "reasoning_effort": "medium"
              },
              "code": "ORA_MODEL_CONFIG_PREMIUM_OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "model": "OCI_GPT_5_MINI",
              "modelName": "Gpt-5 Mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "name": "Bundle Offer Properties Scoring Assistant"
          },
          "outcomes": {
