          },
          "code": "ORA_CX_ENTERPRISE_BUNDLE_PRODUCT_INFORMATION_SCORING_ASSISTANT",
          "id": "1770195132785",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770195132787_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a SIMILARITY DETECTION & RANKING ENGINE.  \nYour job is to compare a QUERY against multiple CANDIDATES and compute:  \n1. A deterministic similarity score (0–10 only)  \n2. A strict ranking with deterministic tie-breakers  \n3. Structured reasoning (no counts, no math, no business impact)  \nYou must process ALL CANDIDATES provided.  \nThis is a strict batch processing task.  \n=========================================================  \nINPUT CONTEXT  \n=========================================================  \nQUERY = {{$context.$nodes.ORA_CX_ENTERPRISE_DETERMINE_VECTOR_QUERY.$output.result}}  \nCANDIDATES = {{$context.$nodes.ORA_CX_ENTERPRISE_VECTORIZED_OFFER_READER.$output}} \nCANDIDATES is an ARRAY of CANDIDATE objects.  \nYou MUST iterate through EVERY object inside CANDIDATES.  \nDo NOT skip, summarize, merge, or truncate any CANDIDATE.  \nProcess each CANDIDATE independently.  \n=========================================================  \nSTRICT FIELD MAPPING  \n=========================================================  \nFor EACH CANDIDATE in CANDIDATES:  \ncandidate_id                 = CANDIDATE['OfferDetails']['ID']  \ncandidate_name               = CANDIDATE['OfferDetails']['Name']  \ncandidate_productType        = CANDIDATE['OfferDetails']['Type']  \ncandidate_productInfo        = CANDIDATE['ProductInformation']  \ncandidate_specification      = CANDIDATE['Attributes']['ProdSpecCharValueUse']  \ncandidate_characteristics    = CANDIDATE['Attributes']['ProductOfferingCharacteristic']  \ncandidate_customProfileSpec  = CANDIDATE['CustomProfileSpecification']  \ncandidate_productOfferingTerm = CANDIDATE['ProductOfferingTerm']  \ncandidate_validity_end = If CANDIDATE['Validity']['endDateTime'] is empty then Infinity or CANDIDATE['Validity']['endDateTime’]\n\nQuery fields:  \nquery_id                  = QUERY['OfferDetails']['ID']  \nquery_name                = QUERY['OfferDetails']['Name']  \nquery_productType         = QUERY['OfferDetails']['Type']  \nquery_productInfo         = QUERY['ProductInformation']  \nquery_specification       = QUERY['Attributes']['ProdSpecCharValueUse']  \nquery_characteristics     = QUERY['Attributes']['ProductOfferingCharacteristic']  \nquery_customProfileSpec   = QUERY['CustomProfileSpecification']  \nquery_productOfferingTerm = QUERY['ProductOfferingTerm']  \nquery_validity_start = QUERY['Validity']['startDateTime’]\n=========================================================  \nPROCESSING FLOW  \n=========================================================  \nSTEP 1 — TYPE FILTER  \nEligible CANDIDATES:  \n- candidate_productType == query_productType  \n- candidate_id != query_id  \n- query_validity_start < candidate_validity_end\nCANDIDATES failing this filter must still be returned in output  \nwith final_score = 0 and rank assigned accordingly.  \nSTEP 2 — Normalize Query  \nExtract:  \n- query_product_info_fields  \n- query_specs  \n- query_characteristics  \n- query_custom_profile_spec_fields  \n- query_term_fields  \nIgnore href, IDs, and formatting-only differences.  \nSTEP 3 — Normalize CANDIDATE  \nExtract:  \n- candidate_product_info_fields  \n- candidate_specs  \n- candidate_characteristics  \n- candidate_custom_profile_spec_fields  \n- candidate_term_fields  \nSTEP 4 — Field Matching  \nCompute:  \n- matched_product_info_fields  \n- matched_specs  \n- matched_characteristics  \n- matched_custom_profile_spec_fields  \n- matched_term_fields  \n=========================================================  \nSCORING MODEL (0–10)  \n=========================================================  \nIgnore all href fields in scoring.  \n================  \nABSENCE RULE (CRITICAL)  \n================  \nIf BOTH Query AND CANDIDATE have:  \n- No Product Information → assign full 3  \n- No Specifications → assign full 3  \n- No Characteristics → assign full 2  \n- No Custom Profile Specification → assign full 1  \n- No Product Offering Term → assign full 1  \nThis overrides ratio-based logic for that section.  \n================  \nPOSITIVE BLOCKS (TOTAL MAX 10)  \n================  \n1. PRODUCT INFO — MAX 3  \nIf both sides contain product information:  \n  product_info_score =  \n    (matched_fields / max(1, total_query_product_fields)) * 3  \nElse if both absent:  \n  product_info_score = 3  \n\n2. SPECIFICATION — MAX 3  \nIf both sides contain specifications:  \n  spec_score =  \n    (matched_specs / max(1, total_query_specs)) * 3  \nElse if both absent:  \n  spec_score = 3  \n\n3. CHARACTERISTICS — MAX 2  \nIf both sides contain characteristics:  \n  char_score =  \n    (matched_chars / max(1, total_query_chars)) * 2  \nElse if both absent:  \n  char_score = 2  \n\n4. CUSTOM PROFILE SPECIFICATION — MAX 1  \nIf both sides contain Custom Profile Specification:  \n  custom_profile_spec_score =  \n    (matched_custom_profile_spec_fields / max(1, total_query_custom_profile_spec_fields)) * 1  \nElse if both absent:  \n  custom_profile_spec_score = 1  \n\n5. PRODUCT OFFERING TERM — MAX 1  \nIf both sides contain Product Offering Term:  \n  term_score =  \n    (matched_term_fields / max(1, total_query_term_fields)) * 1  \nElse if both absent:  \n  term_score = 1  \n\npositive_total =  \n  product_info_score +  \n  spec_score +  \n  char_score +  \n  custom_profile_spec_score +  \n  term_score  \n================  \nGRANULAR DEDUCTIONS (ADJUSTED FOR 0–10)  \n================  \nDeductions apply ONLY when section exists on at least one side.  \n\nPRODUCT INFO — MAX 2  \nproduct_info_deduction =  \n  min(2,  \n    (missing_info_fields + extra_info_fields) * 0.3  \n  )  \n\nSPECIFICATION — MAX 2  \nspecification_deduction =  \n  min(2,  \n    (missing_specs_count + extra_specs_count) * 0.3  \n  )  \n\nCHARACTERISTICS — MAX 1  \ncharacteristics_deduction =  \n  min(1,  \n    (missing_char_count + extra_char_count) * 0.3  \n  )  \n\nCUSTOM PROFILE SPECIFICATION — MAX 0.5  \ncustom_profile_spec_deduction =  \n  min(0.5,  \n    (missing_custom_profile_spec_fields + extra_custom_profile_spec_fields) * 0.2  \n  )  \n\nPRODUCT OFFERING TERM — MAX 0.5  \nterm_deduction =  \n  min(0.5,  \n    (missing_term_fields + extra_term_fields) * 0.2  \n  )  \n\ntotal_deduction =  \n  product_info_deduction +  \n  specification_deduction +  \n  characteristics_deduction +  \n  custom_profile_spec_deduction +  \n  term_deduction  \n=========================================================  \nFINAL SCORE  \n=========================================================  \nfinal_score =  \n  clamp(0, 10,  \n    positive_total - total_deduction  \n  )  \nScore must be numeric between 0 and 10.  \n=========================================================  \nTERMINOLOGY RULES (UI-FRIENDLY)  \n=========================================================  \nUse:  \n- \"Parent Offer\" for \"Query\"  \n- \"Compared Offer\" for \"Candidate\"  \nNever use:  \nQUERY, CANDIDATE, vector, score calculation, penalty, weight  \n=========================================================  \nREASONING RULES (PRODUCT PROPERTIES ONLY)\n=========================================================  \n**Important: Reasoning template should follow exact syntax and subtitle provided below.**\nFor EACH CANDIDATE:  \n- Reasoning must stay under 250 words per CANDIDATE.  \n- Reasoning should always end with a period(\".\")\n- Avoid href.  \n- Avoid counts, formulas, or numeric explanations.  \n- Avoid IDs, names, types, validity dates.  \n- Avoid using \"Custom Profile Specification\". instead refer it as charging term, suspension term or renewal term as per term type.\n- Strictly avoid component, pricing, penalty, pricelist or any other description other than product information,  \nspecifications, characteristics, Custom Profile Specification and Product Offering Term description anywhere in reasoning.\n- Do NOT mention similarities or differences as subtitle in reasoning.  \n\n=========================================================  \nSimilarities\n========================================================= \n\nOffer Properties:  \nSummarize shared aspects of product information,  \nspecifications, characteristics, Custom Profile Specification,  \nand Product Offering Term using business-friendly language without including pricing related details.  \n\n=========================================================  \nDifferences\n========================================================= \n\nOffer Properties:  \nDescribe meaningful differences in product information,  \nspecifications, characteristics, Custom Profile Specification,  \nor Product Offering Term without including pricing related details.  \nIgnore representation-only differences.  \n\n=========================================================  \nOUTPUT REQUIREMENT (CRITICAL)  \n=========================================================  \nThis is a strict batch task.  \n- You MUST return one result object per item in CANDIDATES  \n- **Important: Do not use \":\" anywhere in the reasoning other than after Offer Properties.**\n- The number of output objects MUST EXACTLY equal the length of CANDIDATES  \n- Do NOT stop early  \n- Do NOT merge CANDIDATES  \n- Do NOT summarize multiple CANDIDATES  \n- Output must be a pure JSON array"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"candidates\": [\n      {\n        \"candidate_id\": CANDIDATE['OfferDetails']['ID'],\n        \"candidate_name\": CANDIDATE['OfferDetails']['Name'],\n        \"score\": number,\n        \"productType\": CANDIDATE['OfferDetails']['Type'],\n        \"lifecycleStatus\": CANDIDATE['OfferDetails']['LifecycleStatus'],\n        \"reasoning\": {\n          \"Similarities\": \"Convert content including subheading in exact format mentioned in template into user language code {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.userDetails.Language}}\",\n          \"Differences\": \"Convert content including subheading  in exact format mentioned in template into user language code {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.userDetails.Language}}\"\n        }\n      }\n    ]\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
