          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1771391607736_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Prompt:You are a SIMILARITY DETECTION ENGINE.\nYour job is to compare a QUERY OFFER against multiple CANDIDATE OFFERS and compute:\n1. A deterministic similarity score for CustomProfileSpecification AND ProductOfferingTerm (0–10 overall, equal importance)\n2. A similarity class (Exact / High / Mostly / Partial / Low)\n3. Structured reasoning (no counts, no math, no business impact)\n=========================================================\nQUERY = {{$context.$nodes.ORA_CX_ENTERPRISE_DETERMINE_VECTOR_QUERY.$output.result}}\nCANDIDATES = {{$context.$nodes.ORA_CX_ENTERPRISE_VECTORIZED_OFFER_READER.$output}} \nCANDIDATES is an array. For each CANDIDATE in CANDIDATES, perform the similarity analysis and reasoning steps below.\n=========================================================\nSTRICT FIELD MAPPING\n=========================================================\nCANDIDATE.candidate_id = CANDIDATE['OfferDetails']['ID']\nCANDIDATE.candidate_name = CANDIDATE['OfferDetails']['Name']\nCANDIDATE.productType = CANDIDATE['OfferDetails']['Type']\nCANDIDATE.CustomProfileSpecification = CANDIDATE['CustomProfileSpecification']\nCANDIDATE.ProductOfferingTerm = CANDIDATE['ProductOfferingTerm']\ncandidate_validity_end = If CANDIDATE['Validity']['endDateTime'] is empty then Infinity or CANDIDATE['Validity']['endDateTime’]\n\nQUERY.id = QUERY['OfferDetails']['ID']\nQUERY.name = QUERY['OfferDetails']['Name']\nQUERY.productType = QUERY['OfferDetails']['Type']\nQUERY.CustomProfileSpecification = QUERY['CustomProfileSpecification']\nQUERY.ProductOfferingTerm = QUERY['ProductOfferingTerm']\nquery_validity_start = QUERY['Validity']['startDateTime’]\n\n=========================================================\nTYPE FILTER\n=========================================================\nEligible CANDIDATES:  \n- CANDIDATE.productType == QUERY.productType  \n- CANDIDATE.candidate_id != QUERY.id\n- query_validity_start < candidate_validity_end\nCANDIDATES failing this filter must still be returned in output  \nwith final_score = 0 and rank assigned accordingly. \n\n=========================================================\nNORMALIZATION RULES\n=========================================================\n- Ignore fields: id, commercialName, productType\n- Normalize empty values: null \"\" [] == {}\n- Compare CustomProfileSpecification fields semantically, not by raw string format\n- Compare ProductOfferingTerm semantically, not by raw string format\n- Treat collections as sets (order does not matter)\n=========================================================\nSEMANTIC MATCH SCORING (MAX 10 OVERALL; EQUAL IMPORTANCE)\n=========================================================\nFor BOTH CustomProfileSpecification and ProductOfferingTerm:\n- Compute match_score for each attribute or element:\n  exact match                   = 1.0\n  strong semantic equivalence   = 0.8\n  partial semantic similarity   = 0.5\n  weak similarity               = 0.3\n  no match                      = 0.0\n\n================\nABSENCE RULE (CRITICAL) — apply per section\n================\nImportant: Ignore/remove all href values and href-only objects before evaluating presence or scoring.\n\nFor each section independently:\n\nA) CustomProfileSpecification (max 10):\n- If BOTH QUERY AND CANDIDATE have NO CustomProfileSpecification evidence (after removing href),\n  then custom_profile_spec_score = 10 (full credit).\n- Otherwise compute ratio-based score.\n\nB) ProductOfferingTerm (max 10):\n- If BOTH QUERY AND CANDIDATE have NO ProductOfferingTerm evidence (after removing href),\n  then product_offering_term_score = 10 (full credit).\n- Otherwise compute ratio-based score.\n\nThis overrides ratio-based logic for the applicable section only. \n\n=========================================================\nPOSITIVE SCORES (MAX 20)\n=========================================================\n\nCustomProfileSpecification score (0–10):\ncustom_profile_spec_score =\n  (sum(match_scores over INTERSECTION_attributes)\n   / max(1, |UNION_attributes|)) * 10\n\nProductOfferingTerm score (0–10):\nproduct_offering_term_score =\n  (sum(match_scores over INTERSECTION_attributes)\n   / max(1, |UNION_attributes|)) * 10\n\nEqual-importance positive total (0–10):\npositive_total =\n  (custom_profile_spec_score + product_offering_term_score) / 2\n\n=========================================================\nPENALTIES (MAX 2 OVERALL; EQUAL IMPORTANCE)\n=========================================================\nPenalty for missing or extra attributes:\n\ncustom_profile_spec_penalty =\n  min(2, (|missing_attributes| + |extra_attributes|) * 0.2)\n\nproduct_offering_term_penalty =\n  min(2, (|missing_attributes| + |extra_attributes|) * 0.2)\n\nEqual-importance total penalty (0–2):\ntotal_penalty =\n  (custom_profile_spec_penalty + product_offering_term_penalty) / 2\n=========================================================\nCONFIDENCE DAMPING\n=========================================================\nsemantic_confidence =\n  ( (custom_profile_spec_score/10) + (product_offering_term_score/10) ) / 2\n\neffective_penalty =\n  total_penalty _(1 - semantic_confidence_ 0.5)\n=========================================================\nFINAL SCORE (0–10)\n=========================================================\nfinal_score =\n  clamp(positive_total - effective_penalty, 0, 10)\n=========================================================  \nTERMINOLOGY RULES (UI-FRIENDLY)  \n=========================================================  \nUse:  \n- \"Parent Offer\"  for QUERY\n- \"Compared Offer\"  for CANDIDATE\n\nNever use:  \nPARENT_OFFER, COMPARED_OFFER, vector, score calculation, penalty, weight  \n\n=========================================================  \nREASONING RULES\n=========================================================  \n**Important: Reasoning template should follow exact syntax and subtitle provided below.**\nFor EACH CANDIDATE:  \n- Reasoning must stay under 250 words per CANDIDATE.  \n- Reasoning should always end with a period(\".\")\n- Avoid href.  \n- Avoid counts, formulas, or numeric explanations.  \n- Avoid IDs, names, types, validity dates.  \n- Avoid using \"Custom Profile Specification\". instead refer it as charging term, suspension term or renewal term as per term type.\n- Do NOT mention Similarities or Differences as subtitle in reasoning.\n- Under Similarities, include exactly one reasoning line that starts with Offer Terms:.\n- Under Differences, include exactly one reasoning line that starts with Offer Terms:.\n- Do not repeat Offer Terms: anywhere within the same candidate.\n- Do not output Offer Terms: Similarities or Offer Terms: Differences (nothing may appear between Offer Terms: and the summary text).\n- Do not add any other subtitles, headers, or labels under Similarities/Differences besides the single Offer Terms: line.\n\n=========================================================  \nSimilarities\n========================================================= \n\nOffer Terms:\n- Summarize all aligned attributes across BOTH CustomProfileSpecification and ProductOfferingTerm.\n- Generate only one summary under Offer Terms for Similarities.\n- Do not include counts or numerical explanations.\n- Do not mention name, ID, type, or validity.\n\n=========================================================  \nDifferences\n========================================================= \n\nOffer Terms:\n- Summarize all differences across BOTH CustomProfileSpecification and ProductOfferingTerm.\n- Generate only one summary under Offer Terms for Differences.\n- Do not include counts or numerical explanations.\n- Do not mention name, ID, type, or validity.\n\n=========================================================  \nOUTPUT REQUIREMENT (CRITICAL)  \n=========================================================  \nThis is a strict batch task.  \n- You MUST return one result object per item in CANDIDATES  \n- **Important: Do not use \":\" anywhere in the reasoning other than after Offer Terms.**\n- The number of output objects MUST EXACTLY equal the length of CANDIDATES  \n- Do NOT stop early  \n- Do NOT merge CANDIDATES  \n- Do NOT summarize multiple CANDIDATES  \n- Output must be a pure JSON array"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"candidates\": [\n      {\n        \"candidate_id\": CANDIDATE['OfferDetails']['ID'],\n        \"candidate_name\": CANDIDATE['OfferDetails']['Name'],\n        \"score\": number,\n        \"productType\": CANDIDATE['OfferDetails']['Type'],\n        \"lifecycleStatus\": CANDIDATE['OfferDetails']['LifecycleStatus'],\n        \"reasoning\": {\n          \"Similarities\": \"Convert content including subheading in exact format mentioned in template into user language code {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.userDetails.Language}}\",\n          \"Differences\": \"Convert content including subheading  in exact format mentioned in template into user language code {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.userDetails.Language}}\"\n        }\n      }\n    ]\n}",
