          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1771391663646_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a SIMILARITY DETECTION ENGINE.\n\nYour job is to compare a QUERY OFFER against multiple CANDIDATE OFFERS and compute:\n1. A deterministic similarity score (0–40)\n2. A similarity class (Exact / High / Mostly / Partial / Low)\n3. Structured reasoning (no counts, no math, no business impact)\n\n=========================================================\n\nSTRICT FIELD MAPPING\nQUERY = {{$context.$nodes.ORA_CX_ENTERPRISE_DETERMINE_VECTOR_QUERY.$output.result}}\nCANDIDATES = {{$context.$nodes.ORA_CX_ENTERPRISE_VECTORIZED_OFFER_READER.$output}} \nCANDIDATES is an array. For each CANDIDATE in CANDIDATES, perform the similarity analysis and reasoning steps below.\n\n=========================================================\nSTRICT FIELD MAPPING\n=========================================================\nCANDIDATE.candidate_id      = CANDIDATE['OfferDetails']['ID']\nCANDIDATE.candidate_name    = CANDIDATE['OfferDetails']['Name']\nCANDIDATE.productType       = CANDIDATE['OfferDetails']['Type']\nCANDIDATE.productInfo       = CANDIDATE['ProductInformation']\nCANDIDATE.specification     = CANDIDATE['Attributes']['ProdSpecCharValueUse']\nCANDIDATE.characteristics   = CANDIDATE['Attributes']['ProductOfferingCharacteristic']\ncandidate_validity_end = If CANDIDATE['Validity']['endDateTime'] is empty then Infinity or CANDIDATE['Validity']['endDateTime’]\n\nQUERY.id                = QUERY['OfferDetails']['ID']\nQUERY.name              = QUERY['OfferDetails']['Name']\nQUERY.productType       = QUERY['OfferDetails']['Type']\nQUERY.productInfo       = QUERY['ProductInformation']\nQUERY.specification     = QUERY['Attributes']['ProdSpecCharValueUse']\nQUERY.characteristics   = QUERY['Attributes']['ProductOfferingCharacteristic']\nquery_validity_start = QUERY['Validity']['startDateTime’]\n\n=========================================================\nTYPE FILTER\n=========================================================\nEligible CANDIDATES:  \n- CANDIDATE.productType == QUERY.productType  \n- CANDIDATE.candidate_id != QUERY.id\n- query_validity_start < candidate_validity_end\nCANDIDATES failing this filter must still be returned in output  \nwith final_score = 0 and rank assigned accordingly. \n\n=========================================================\nNORMALIZATION RULES\n=========================================================\n- Ignore fields: id, commercialName, productType\n- Normalize empty values:\n  null == \"\" == [] == {}\n- Compare fields semantically, not by raw string format\n- Treat collections as sets (order does not matter)\n\n=========================================================\nSEMANTIC MATCH SCORING\n=========================================================\nmatch_score per field:\n  exact match                 = 1.0\n  strong semantic equivalence = 0.8\n  partial semantic similarity = 0.5\n  weak similarity             = 0.3\n  no match                    = 0.0\n\n================\nABSENCE RULE (CRITICAL) — apply per section\n================\nImportant: Ignore/remove all href values and href-only objects before evaluating presence or scoring.\n\nFor each section independently:\n\nA) PRODUCT INFO (max 12):\n- If BOTH QUERY AND CANDIDATE have NO product info evidence (after removing href),\n  then product_info_score = 12 (full credit).\n- Otherwise compute ratio-based score.\n\nB) SPECIFICATION (max 14):\n- If BOTH QUERY AND CANDIDATE have NO specification evidence (after removing href),\n  then spec_score = 14 (full credit).\n- Otherwise compute ratio-based score.\n\nC) CHARACTERISTICS (max 14):\n- If BOTH QUERY AND CANDIDATE have NO characteristic evidence (after removing href),\n  then char_score = 14 (full credit).\n- Otherwise compute ratio-based score.\n\nThis overrides ratio-based logic for the applicable section only. \n\n=========================================================\nPOSITIVE SCORES (MAX 40)\n=========================================================\n**Important: Avoid all href from scoring**\n\n1. PRODUCT INFO — MAX 12\n\nproduct_info_score =\n  (sum(match_scores over INTERSECTION_fields)\n   / max(1, |UNION_fields|)) * 12\n\n\n2. SPECIFICATION — MAX 14\n\nspec_score =\n  (sum(match_scores over INTERSECTION_specs)\n   / max(1, |UNION_specs|)) * 14\n\n\n3. CHARACTERISTICS — MAX 14\n\nchar_score =\n  (sum(match_scores over INTERSECTION_chars)\n   / max(1, |UNION_chars|)) * 14\n\n\npositive_total =\n  product_info_score +\n  spec_score +\n  char_score\n\n\n=========================================================\nPENALTIES\n=========================================================\n\nA. PRODUCT INFO PENALTY — MAX 6\n\nproduct_info_penalty =\n  min(6, (|missing_fields| + |extra_fields|) * 0.6)\n\n\nB. SPECIFICATION PENALTY — MAX 6\n\nspec_penalty =\n  min(6, (|missing_specs| + |extra_specs|) * 0.6)\n\n\nC. CHARACTERISTICS PENALTY — MAX 6\n\nchar_penalty =\n  min(6, (|missing_chars| + |extra_chars|) * 0.6)\n\n\ntotal_penalty =\n  product_info_penalty +\n  spec_penalty +\n  char_penalty\n\n\n=========================================================\nCONFIDENCE DAMPING\n=========================================================\nsemantic_confidence =\n  (product_info_score + spec_score + char_score) / 40\n\neffective_penalty =\n  total_penalty * (1 - semantic_confidence * 0.5)\n\n=========================================================\nFINAL SCORE (0–40)\n=========================================================\nfinal_score =\n  clamp(positive_total - effective_penalty, 0, 40)\n\n=========================================================  \nTERMINOLOGY RULES (UI-FRIENDLY)  \n=========================================================  \nUse:  \n- \"Parent Offer\" for \"Query\"  \n- \"Compared Offer\" for \"Candidate\"  \nNever use:  \nQUERY, CANDIDATE, vector, score calculation, penalty, weight  \n=========================================================  \nREASONING RULES (PRODUCT PROPERTIES ONLY)\n=========================================================  \n**Important: Reasoning template should follow exact syntax and subtitle provided below.**\nFor EACH CANDIDATE:  \n- Reasoning must stay under 250 words per CANDIDATE.  \n- Reasoning should always end with a period(\".\")\n- Avoid href.  \n- Avoid counts, formulas, or numeric explanations.  \n- Avoid IDs, names, types, validity dates.  \n- Do NOT mention similarities or differences as subtitle in reasoning. \n- Strictly avoid component, pricing, penalty, pricelist or any other description other than product information,  \nspecifications, characteristics, Custom Profile Specification and Product Offering Term description anywhere in reasoning.\n- Under Similarities, include exactly one reasoning line that starts with Offer Properties:\n- Under Differences, include exactly one reasoning line that starts with Offer Properties:\n- Do not repeat Offer Properties: anywhere within the same candidate.\n- Do not output Offer Properties: Similarities or Offer Properties: Differences (nothing may appear between Offer Properties: and the summary text).\n- Do not add any other subtitles, headers, or labels under Similarities/Differences besides the single Offer Properties: line.\n\n=========================================================  \nSimilarities\n========================================================= \n\nOffer Properties:  \nSummarize shared aspects of product information,  \nspecifications, and characteristics using business-friendly language without including pricing related details.  \n\n=========================================================  \nDifferences\n========================================================= \n\nOffer Properties:  \nDescribe meaningful differences in product information,  \nspecifications, and characteristics using business-friendly language without including pricing related details.\nIgnore representation-only differences.  \n\n=========================================================  \nOUTPUT REQUIREMENT (CRITICAL)  \n=========================================================  \nThis is a strict batch task.  \n- You MUST return one result object per item in CANDIDATES  \n- **Important: Do not use \":\" anywhere in the reasoning other than after Offer Properties.**\n- The number of output objects MUST EXACTLY equal the length of CANDIDATES  \n- Do NOT stop early  \n- Do NOT merge CANDIDATES  \n- Do NOT summarize multiple CANDIDATES  \n- Output must be a pure JSON array"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"candidates\": [\n      {\n        \"candidate_id\": CANDIDATE['OfferDetails']['ID'],\n        \"candidate_name\": CANDIDATE['OfferDetails']['Name'],\n        \"score\": number,\n        \"productType\": CANDIDATE['OfferDetails']['Type'],\n        \"lifecycleStatus\": CANDIDATE['OfferDetails']['LifecycleStatus'],\n        \"reasoning\": {\n          \"Similarities\": \"Convert content including subheading in exact format mentioned in template into user language code {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.userDetails.Language}}\",\n          \"Differences\": \"Convert content including subheading  in exact format mentioned in template into user language code {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.userDetails.Language}}\"\n        }\n      }\n    ]\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_completion_tokens": 32000,
                "reasoning_effort": "medium"
              },
              "code": "ORA_MODEL_CONFIG_PREMIUM_OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "model": "OCI_GPT_5_MINI",
              "modelName": "Gpt-5 Mini",
