                {
                  "metadata": {
                    "name": "Product Offering Price Summarizer for Offers"
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "success": "1775578325373"
                  },
                  "code": "ORA_CX_ENTERPRISE_PRODUCT_OFFERING_PRICE_SUMMARIZER_FOR_OFFERS",
                  "id": "1775578248760",
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "1775578248761_1",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "You are an expert in TM Forum Open APIs (TMF) v5 ProductOfferingPrice payloads (including Oracle extensions).\n\nGOAL\nGiven a JSON payload that contains a top-level array field `productOfferingPrice`, output EXACTLY ONE LINE that can be used for comparison. The summary MUST include all relevant ProductOfferingPrice details from the payload, BUT must OMIT `project` and `pricelist` because those are repetitive and will be sourced from the offer top-level.\n\nABSOLUTE OUTPUT RULES\n1) Output must be exactly ONE LINE (no newline characters).\n2) Do NOT add any prefix/heading and do NOT add any leading/trailing stray characters (no quotes like ', no commas, no brackets).\n   - The output must begin with `id=` of the first element and end with the last key/value pair of the last element.\n3) Use ONLY these separators:\n   - Between key/value pairs within an element: ` | ` (space-pipe-space)\n4) NEVER use commas as separators. NEVER output `| |`. NEVER output trailing separators.\n\nELEMENT IDENTIFICATION (required)\n- Each element block MUST begin with (in this exact order):\n  1) `id=<value>`\n  2) `name=<value>`\n- Then include all remaining included fields for that element.\n\nFIELDS TO OMIT (important)\n- Omit `project` entirely (do not output `project.*` anywhere).\n- Omit `pricelist` entirely (do not output `pricelist[*].*` anywhere).\n- Do not mention omitted fields in the output (no placeholders, no “omitted” notes).\n\nWHAT TO INCLUDE (everything else present in payload)\nFor EACH ProductOfferingPrice element, include EVERY field that exists in the element EXCEPT the omitted fields above, including:\n- Scalars: `description`, `version`, `priceType`, `priceSubType`, `lifecycleStatus`, `isBundle`, `isTaxInclusive`, `percentage`, `alterationType`, `oneTimeFeeType`, `recurringFeeType`, `recurringChargePeriodType`, `recurringChargePeriodLength`, `discountable`, `billOnPurchase`, `shareAllowance`, `usageUnit`, etc.\n- Meta/extension fields wherever present: `@type`, `@baseType`, `@schemaLocation`, `@referredType`\n- Nested objects/arrays (fully expanded with indices), including but not limited to:\n  - `validFor.*`\n  - `price.*`\n  - `unitOfMeasure.*`\n  - `allowanceValidity.*`\n  - `prorationReductionTerm[*].*`\n  - `balanceElement[*].*`\n  - `popAssociation.*`\n  - `bundledPopRelationship[*].*`\n  - `popRelationship[*].*`\n  - `compositePopRelationship[*].*` (each embedded object fully expanded; also apply the same omit rules inside embedded objects: omit any `project.*` and `pricelist[*].*` if present there)\n  - `usageSpecMeteringRuleUse[*].*` including nested `usageSpecification.*`\n  - `usageSpecification.*`\n  - `policy[*].*` including:\n    - `policy[*].specCharUse[*].*`\n    - `policy[*].policyActionRelationship[*].*` (ALL entries, including `constraint.*` and `policyAction.*`)\n    - `policy[*].valueMap.*`\n  (Also apply omit rules inside all nested structures: omit any `project.*` and `pricelist[*].*` encountered anywhere.)\n\nKEY/PATH RULES (must preserve structure)\n- Do NOT use `$` or JSONPath roots.\n- Use fully-qualified keys relative to the current ProductOfferingPrice element, using dot notation and explicit array indices.\n- Preserve true JSON structure; do not move fields under wrong parents.\n  Example: `policy[0].policyActionRelationship[0].constraint.id=...` is valid.\n  Do NOT output `policy[0].policyActionRelationship[0].policyAction.constraint...`.\n\nVALUE FORMATTING\n- Strings: output exactly as in JSON.\n  - Only wrap in double quotes if the string contains ` | ` or has leading/trailing spaces.\n  - Escape internal double quotes with backslash.\n- Numbers/booleans: output JSON literals (preserve decimal formatting as in input if possible).\n- If a field exists and is null: `field=null`\n- If a field exists and is an empty array/object: `field=[]` or `field={}`\n- Do not reformat timestamps/dates.\n\nORDERING (deterministic)\n- Within each element, emit fields in the same order they appear in the input JSON (top-to-bottom),\n  except `id` and `name` which must be emitted first.\n- For arrays, emit elements in index order; within each element preserve field order.\n\nFINAL VALIDATION (must perform before output)\n- Confirm each element starts with `id=...|name=...`.\n- Confirm there are NO commas used as separators and no stray leading/trailing quotes.\n- Confirm NO `project.*` or `pricelist[*].*` appears anywhere in the output.\n- Confirm output is a single line.\n\nNow generate the one-line summary for this payload:\n```json\n {{$context.$nodes.ORA_CX_ENTERPRISE_PRODUCT_OFFERING_PRICE_CHUNKS_ITERATOR.$currentItem}}"
                    }
                  ],
                  "type": "LLM"
                },
