            "name": "Product Offering Price Plan Relationship Summarizer for Offers"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1775580702873"
          },
          "code": "ORA_CX_ENTERPRISE_PRODUCT_OFFERING_PRICE_PLAN_RELATIONSHIP_SUMMARIZER_FOR_OFFERS",
          "id": "1775579691327",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775579691328_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are given a JSON payload that contains a `pricePlanRelationship` array.\nTask:\nGenerate a JSON array of one-line summary strings. Create exactly one string per `pricePlanRelationship` object (preserve original order).\nOutput must be valid JSON only (no prose, no markdown).\nDo NOT include these repetitive/noise fields anywhere in the summary:\n- Any `version`\n- Any `@type`\n- Any `@referredType`\nOne-line output format (exact separators):\n\"<PPR_ID> | <PPR_NAME> | rel=[...] | scope={...}\"\n------------------------------------------------------------\nA) rel=[...]\nIf `popRelationship` exists and is non-empty:\n1) Sort popRelationship entries by `relationshipType` (asc), then `id` (asc)\n2) Build:\n   rel=[<RELTYPE>:<ID>(<NAME>){seq=<sequential>,mode=<discountMode>}, ...]\n- Include `{...}` only if at least one of `sequential` or `discountMode` exists.\n- Inside `{...}`:\n  - include `seq=<sequential>` only if `sequential` exists\n  - include `mode=<discountMode>` only if `discountMode` exists\nElse:\nrel=[]\n------------------------------------------------------------\nB) scope={...}\nStart with an empty set of scope fragments. Join fragments with \"; \" inside scope={...}.\nIf there are no fragments at all, output: scope={}\n1) appliesTo\n- If `appliesTo` exists and after trimming is non-empty:\n  add fragment: \"appliesTo=<appliesTo>\"\n2) applicableOfferings\n  a) Sort offerings by `id` (asc)\n  b) applicableOfferings fragment (always included when array exists/non-empty):\n     \"applicableOfferings=[<OFF_ID>(<OFF_NAME>){poh=<POH_OR_EMPTY>; rh=<RH_OR_EMPTY>}, ...]\"\n     Where for EACH offering:\n     - Read `productOfferingHierarchy` ONLY from:\n       applicableProductOffering[0].productOfferingHierarchy\n     - Read `relationshipHierarchy` ONLY from:\n       applicableProductOffering[0].relationshipHierarchy\n     - Define non-empty string as: field exists AND trim(value).length > 0\n     - POH_OR_EMPTY:\n       - if applicableProductOffering[0].productOfferingHierarchy is non-empty => use the exact value verbatim\n       - else => ''  (two single-quotes)\n     - RH_OR_EMPTY:\n       - if applicableProductOffering[0].relationshipHierarchy is non-empty => use the exact value verbatim\n       - else => ''  (two single-quotes)\n     - Always include BOTH keys in this exact order: `poh` then `rh`\n     - Do not infer, fabricate, or copy these values from any other field/path.\n------------------------------------------------------------\nInput JSON:\n{{$context.$variables.offerPayloadPPR}}\nReturn only the JSON array of one-line summary strings.\n\n\n**Important: Strictly follow String Content Structure. Include only correct information. If Input JSON is empty then return ''**"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Product Offering Pricelist Summarizer for Offers"
